---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config";

const updated = "October 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`privacy · ${site.name}`}
  description={`how ${site.name} handles data, visitors, and third-party services.`}
>
  <main class="page">
    <article class="doc card" data-reveal>
      <a class="back" href="/">← back</a>
      <h1>privacy</h1>
      <p class="updated">last updated {updated}</p>

      <section>
        <h2>overview</h2>
        <p>
          this site is a personal portfolio. it exists to show who {site.name}
          is and what they build. it is designed to collect as little as
          possible, and nothing here is used to build a profile of you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>visitor count</h2>
        <p>
          the home page shows a visitor count. each page view of the home page
          sends one request to a counter that adds a single number to a running
          total, stored as one integer row in a hosted postgres database
          (supabase). the counter stores an aggregate integer only. it does not
          store your IP address, browser, location, or any identifier that
          could single you out. the number is not tied to you, and it cannot be
          used to track you between pages or visits.
        </p>
        <p>
          the site also keeps aggregate page view counts, grouped by day and by
          path, so the owner can see which pages are visited in a private admin
          dashboard. these are counts only and contain no personal data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>guestbook</h2>
        <p>
          the guestbook lets you leave a name and a message. when you submit,
          that name and message are stored in the site database and shown
          publicly on the home page, so do not include anything private. entries
          can be upvoted or downvoted, and to stop one person from voting many
          times the site stores one vote per entry against a salted hash of your
          ip address. the raw ip is never stored, and the hash is used only to
          prevent duplicate votes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>rate limits</h2>
        <p>
          to stop spam and abuse, the site limits how often you can post and
          vote. those checks use the anonymous cookie id and a short lived,
          salted hash of your ip address. the hash is used only to enforce the
          limit, it is not reversible to your ip, and it is never linked to your
          entries or votes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>cookies</h2>
        <p>
          the site sets one cookie, lunynt_vid. it is a random value stored on
          your device so you cannot vote twice on the same entry and so the rate
          limits work. it contains no personal data, is not used for tracking,
          and lasts about two years.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>human check</h2>
        <p>
          before you post or vote, a small check asks you to confirm you are
          human. it is handled entirely by this site and uses no third-party
          service, so no data about you is sent anywhere for it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>discord presence</h2>
        <p>
          the currently section uses lanyard, a public service, to show the
          owner's discord status. when you load the page, your browser requests
          that public status from the lanyard api. lanyard may see your IP
          address as part of serving that request, the same way any website you
          contact would. no data about you is stored by this site as a result.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>hosting</h2>
        <p>
          this site is hosted on vercel. like most hosts, vercel records
          standard request logs to run and secure the service. those logs are
          managed by vercel under their own policies and are not used by this
          site for analytics.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>what this site does not do</h2>
        <p>
          no accounts, no cookies, no advertising, no third-party analytics, no
          cross-site tracking, and no fingerprinting. nothing is sold or shared.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>changes</h2>
        <p>
          if this policy changes, the date at the top will be updated. continued
          use of the site after a change means you accept the updated policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>contact</h2>
        <p>
          for any question about this policy, reach out through the public
          channels listed on the home page.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    min-height: 100dvh;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .doc {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 42rem;
    align-self: start;
    padding: 2rem 1.75rem 2.25rem;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }

  .back:hover {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  h1 {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--color-faint);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  p {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
